  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A body falling under gravity covers two points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> separated by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The distance of upper point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> from the starting point is _____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "45",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e9a39584-defd-4a0c-adff-f8a9a61e80ab.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 294px;\"/></p><p>From <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>, using the equation of motion, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math></p><p>From <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>, it follows that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>S</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mn>30</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>)</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mn>900</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi>S</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
